This extension adds Wolfenstein (2009) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Base Folder mods are recognised by a "base" folder.[/*]
[*]Maps mods are recognised by a "maps" folder.[/*]
[*]Stream Packs mods are recognised by a "streampacks" folder.[/*]
[*]Videos mods are recognised by a "videos" folder.[/*]
[*]PK4 mods are recognised by a ".pk4" file.[/*]
[*]Executable mods are recognised by a ".exe" file.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

Some things to note:
[list]
[*]Includes a tool to launch the game with the following command line arguments: '+set com_allowconsole 1 +set com_skipIntro 1 +set com_SingleDeclFile 0 +set sys_lang "english"'[/*]
[*]Default mod install location is by singleplayer .exe ("SP" folder)[/*]
[*]Includes mod types for the root game folder and the multiplayer "MP" folder. [/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Wolfenstein (2009) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Base:

Recognised when the archive contains a "base" folder.

========================================================================

Maps:

Recognised when the archive contains a "maps" folder.

========================================================================

Streampacks:

Recognised when the archive contains a "streampacks" folder.

========================================================================

Videos:

Recognised when the archive contains a "videos" folder.

========================================================================

Pk4:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".pk4" file.

========================================================================

Exe:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".exe" file.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

